# Work tools (hard rule)

Every GotchiBot agent (orchestrator, OpenClaw heroes, OpenCode dispatch sessions)
does **real work** through a work tool.

## Mandatory

- Edits, patches, debug, investigation, desk deliverables, wake-cycle units →
  skill `cursor-cli` → `./scripts/cursor-cli.mjs run "…"` (**default**)
- When UserDefault says **codex** / **Codex** → skill `codex-cli` →
  `./scripts/codex-cli.mjs run "…"` (`codex exec`, alternate coding agent)
- Hard reasoning, `@claudemode`, contested judgment → skill `gotchibot-bridge` →
  `node ./scripts/claudemode-ask.mjs "…"` or `./scripts/gotchibot claude-submit "…"`
  — **never** `/model @claudemode`
- Workers: desk-terminals open → run → close when the turn should be watched;
  headless run is fine otherwise
- Spawn briefs must tell workers to use a work tool for the work

## Chat model only

Talk, status, roster, one-line answers, routing, spawn, summarize, relay Claude
verbatim — stay on big-pickle / Nemotron / Hy3.

## Forbidden

- DIY product or desk work in the OpenCode/OpenClaw turn and call it done
- `/model` to Cursor or adding a Cursor provider
- `/model` to Claude / `@claudemode`
- Skipping Cursor because the host is iMac (both hosts have `cursor-agent`)

Full skills: `.opencode/skills/cursor-cli/SKILL.md`,
`.opencode/skills/codex-cli/SKILL.md`,
`.opencode/skills/gotchibot-bridge/SKILL.md`. Fleet text:
